#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329695 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161965 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "21f1ec99-e166-5986-a07d-f07be0dfeb31" :knowledge-point/title "Using Row Operations to Create a Column of Zeros in a 4x4 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0166ede7-ac8b-5aee-a3fc-ae0a17866fce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+4{R}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{4}:={R}_{4}-3{R}_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326949} {:answer/id #uuid "2ccc7768-32ec-5947-9670-1ec97e53d1da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+4{R}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{4}:={R}_{4}+3{R}_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327328} {:answer/id #uuid "54c6de8d-19a8-57aa-96b2-7a92b017ceaa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-4{R}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{4}:={R}_{4}+3{R}_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327667} {:answer/id #uuid "57b8eae7-5346-50fa-98a2-5cd486bfdba3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-4{R}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{4}:={R}_{4}-3{R}_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327701} {:answer/id #uuid "ddddd82a-3c70-51bf-a2eb-edddccc2e4c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+3{R}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{4}:={R}_{4}-4{R}_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328873}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0166ede7-ac8b-5aee-a3fc-ae0a17866fce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+4{R}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{4}:={R}_{4}-3{R}_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326949} :answer-field/id #uuid "326f90b0-553c-55c5-999d-072fa4528fa2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329280}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5b4f6183-748c-523a-a6b7-35464ca87075" :question/math-academy-id "q-42918" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 4 & -3 & -1 & -6\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 21 & 17 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -8 & -5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 4 & -18 & -13 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices $A$ and $B$ above. By applying three matrix elementary row operations \n\n- ${R}_{1}:=…$\n- ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-2{R}_{3}$\n- ${R}_{4}:=…$\n\neach of the form ${R}_{i}:={R}_{i}+k{R}_{3},$ the matrix $A$ can be transformed into the matrix $B.$ What are the missing elementary row operations?" :question/worked-solution "To transform $A$ into $B,$ we need to make entries above and below ${a}_{34}=-2$ equal to $0.$\n\nTo do this, we can apply the following elementary row operations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 4 & -3 & -1 & -6\\end{aligned}] &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+4{R}_{3}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 21 & 17 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 4 & -3 & -1 & -6\\end{aligned}] &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-2{R}_{3}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 21 & 17 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -8 & -5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 4 & -3 & -1 & -6\\end{aligned}] &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{4}:={R}_{4}-3{R}_{3}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 21 & 17 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -8 & -5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 4 & -18 & -13 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =B.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nTherefore, the missing elementary row operations are\n\n$\\,$ ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+4{R}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{4}:={R}_{4}-3{R}_{3}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162571 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161965 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "21f1ec99-e166-5986-a07d-f07be0dfeb31" :knowledge-point/title "Using Row Operations to Create a Column of Zeros in a 4x4 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "39feaea9-f53d-5ee3-a622-cbfc2b43387f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-{R}_{1}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{4}:={R}_{4}+2{R}_{1}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412015} {:answer/id #uuid "3b22a6a4-61fa-5183-9649-c580b3bc7020" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-{R}_{1}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{4}:={R}_{4}-2{R}_{1}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412016} {:answer/id #uuid "a66beb93-cf63-56e5-af86-8bf4482be7a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-{R}_{1}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{4}:={R}_{4}+{R}_{1}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412019} {:answer/id #uuid "c49a7ab3-b457-50a7-8db3-96d09691584e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+{R}_{1}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{4}:={R}_{4}-2{R}_{1}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412022} {:answer/id #uuid "caaba1b9-461d-5d04-a1fd-8f442d709eb4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+{R}_{1}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{4}:={R}_{4}+2{R}_{1}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412023}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "39feaea9-f53d-5ee3-a622-cbfc2b43387f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-{R}_{1}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{4}:={R}_{4}+2{R}_{1}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412015} :answer-field/id #uuid "db7b0ab2-ace0-5e5f-813e-a09b5ee8870d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412025}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e471ec15-a8b3-57bf-a5ff-3531b5523c10" :question/math-academy-id "q-91171" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -7 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 10 & 7 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 8 & 7 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 0 & 9\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -7 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 13 & 14 & 7 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -5 & -14 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices $A$ and $B$ above. By applying three matrix elementary row operations \n\n- ${R}_{2}:=…$\n- ${R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+{R}_{1}$\n- ${R}_{4}:=…$\n\neach of the form ${R}_{i}:={R}_{i}+k{R}_{1},$ the matrix $A$ can be transformed into the matrix $B.$ What are the missing elementary row operations?" :question/worked-solution "To transform $A$ into $B,$ we need to make entries below ${a}_{11}=1$ equal to $0.$\n\nTo do this, we can apply the following elementary row operations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -7 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 10 & 7 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 8 & 7 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 0 & 9\\end{aligned}] &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -7 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 13 & 14 & 7 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 8 & 7 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 0 & 9\\end{aligned}] &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -7 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 13 & 14 & 7 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 0 & 9\\end{aligned}] &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{4}:={R}_{4}+2{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -7 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 13 & 14 & 7 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -5 & -14 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =B\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nTherefore, the missing elementary row operations are\n\n$\\,$ ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-{R}_{1}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{4}:={R}_{4}+2{R}_{1}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186412026 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161968 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "85e1fe3f-e85e-5ab4-a594-c55b84bb789a" :knowledge-point/title "Using Column Operations to Create a Row of Zeros in a 3x3 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "166feab7-a264-55aa-acc5-4218b97966a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${C}_{2}:={C}_{2}-2{C}_{1}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{3}:={C}_{3}+{C}_{1}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412014} {:answer/id #uuid "4c552dee-9870-5f80-99c4-13a42caad182" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${C}_{2}:={C}_{2}+3{C}_{1}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{3}:={C}_{3}+2{C}_{1}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412017} {:answer/id #uuid "99b872c0-2012-5d57-9afd-16e6b6bde53b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${C}_{2}:={C}_{2}+2{C}_{1}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{3}:={C}_{3}-{C}_{1}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412018} {:answer/id #uuid "a66ce929-c767-5507-b64f-0b3826324583" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${C}_{2}:={C}_{2}-{C}_{1}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{3}:={C}_{3}-2{C}_{1}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412020} {:answer/id #uuid "aa1f46ac-844a-5bb2-b9b6-04cb4156fcf9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${C}_{2}:={C}_{2}-2{C}_{1}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{3}:={C}_{3}-{C}_{1}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412021}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aa1f46ac-844a-5bb2-b9b6-04cb4156fcf9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${C}_{2}:={C}_{2}-2{C}_{1}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{3}:={C}_{3}-{C}_{1}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412021} :answer-field/id #uuid "3ff26ed5-7a58-584f-95b3-0a0e85d61774" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412024}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e8820685-174a-5aac-b0a4-a6b54f80941e" :question/math-academy-id "q-91188" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 7 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 6 & 3\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nBy applying elementary column operations of the form ${C}_{i}:={C}_{i}+k{C}_{1},$ the matrix $A$ can be transformed into the matrix $B.$ What are the elementary column operations?" :question/worked-solution "To transform $A$ into $B,$ we need to make entries to the right of ${a}_{31}=3$ equal to $0.$\n\nTo do this, we can apply the following elementary column operations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 7 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 6 & 3\\end{aligned}] &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{2}:={C}_{2}-2{C}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}] &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{3}:={C}_{3}-{C}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =B\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the elementary column operations are\n\n$\\,$ ${C}_{2}:={C}_{2}-2{C}_{1}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{3}:={C}_{3}-{C}_{1}.$"}]}
